    "why_barefoot": {
      "type": "ls-editorial",
      "settings": {
        "subtitle": "Why Barefoot",
        "heading_line_1": "Toes were meant to",
        "heading_line_2": "spread out.",
        "body": "<p>Children's feet are still developing. Rigid, narrow shoes can restrict natural growth and weaken the muscles that support healthy arches. Barefoot shoes give little feet the freedom to move, grip, and grow the way nature intended.</p>",
        "spec_text": "<p>Wide toe box · zero drop · 5.5 mm flexible sole · no arch support.</p>",
        "spec_text_2": "",
        "image_position": "right",
        "show_floating_icon": true,
        "icon_flip": false,
        "icon_bottom": false,
        "icon_rotation": 0,
        "background_color": "",
        "padding_top": 48,
        "padding_bottom": 48
      }
    },
    "the_pocket": {
      "type": "ls-editorial",
      "settings": {
        "subtitle": "The Pocket",
        "heading_line_1": "A shoe",
        "heading_line_2": "locator.",
        "body": "<p>Choobies feature a built-in, AirTag-compatible compartment designed to help parents quickly find a missing shoe when life gets chaotic. The compartment keeps the AirTag enclosed, secure, and comfortably away from the foot.</p>",
        "spec_text": "<p>\"An AirTag is designed to help locate belongings. Apple and AirTag are trademarks of Apple, Inc. Choobies is not endorsed, sponsored by or affiliated with Apple Inc.\"</p>",
        "spec_text_2": "",
        "image_position": "left",
        "show_floating_icon": true,
        "icon_flip": true,
        "icon_bottom": true,
        "icon_rotation": 0,
        "background_color": "",
        "padding_top": 48,
        "padding_bottom": 48
      }
    },
    "the_research": {
      "type": "ls-editorial",
      "settings": {
        "subtitle": "The Research",
        "heading_line_1": "Why This Matters for Parents.",
        "heading_line_2": "",
        "body": "<p>Children's feet are not miniature adult feet. They're soft, malleable, and rapidly developing.<br><strong>Barefoot shoes:</strong></p><ul><li>Protect without restricting</li><li>Encourage natural sensory feedback</li><li>Support lifelong healthy movement patterns</li></ul><p>Two studies worth reading:</p>",
        "spec_text": "<p><strong>Habitually Barefoot vs. Shod Children</strong><br>Nature · Scientific Reports - <a href=\"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41598-017-07868-4\" target=\"_blank\">Hollander et al., 2017↗</a></p>",
        "spec_text_2": "<p><strong>Barefoot or Shod? Footwear & Children's Gait</strong><br>Applied Sciences (MDPI) - <a href=\"https://www.mdpi.com/2076-3417/16/1/286\" target=\"_blank\">Systematic Review, 2026↗</a></p>",
        "image_position": "right",
        "show_floating_icon": true,
        "icon_flip": false,
        "icon_bottom": true,
        "icon_rotation": 0,
        "background_color": "",
        "padding_top": 48,
        "padding_bottom": 48
      }
    },
